# A suspected creature that loses all abilities loses menace and "This creature can't block" but stays suspected (Case of
# the Stashed Skeleton's rulings; CR 701.60b-c, 613.1f). On turn 2 Bot2's The Wondrous Wasp taps the suspected Skeleton and
# takes its abilities: it has no keywords, but it is still suspected, so at Bot1's turn-3 end step "To solve - You control no
# suspected Skeletons" does not trigger. On turn 4 the Skeleton blocks Bot2's Llanowar Elves (it can block now) and both die;
# at the turn-5 end step Bot1 controls no suspected Skeleton and the Case becomes solved.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Case of the Stashed Skeleton
Swamp x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
The Wondrous Wasp
Llanowar Elves
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Case of the Stashed Skeleton.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.The Wondrous Wasp.Cast
Bot2.Target(Skeleton Token)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Skeleton Token.Suspected = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Skeleton Token.Keywords = (absent)
[T3 Bot1.End]
? Stack.Count = 0
[T4 Bot2.DeclareAttackers]
Bot2.Attack(Llanowar Elves > Bot1)
Bot1.Block(Skeleton Token > Llanowar Elves)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Case of the Stashed Skeleton.Solved = (absent)
[T5 Bot1.End]
? Stack.Count = 1

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Case of the Stashed Skeleton; Mox Jet; Swamp
Bot1.Battlefield.Case of the Stashed Skeleton.Solved = true
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves
Bot2.Battlefield = Island; Mox Emerald; Mox Sapphire; The Wondrous Wasp
Bot1.Life = 20
